SUBROUTINE MATJSONENCODE(MAT A, SPEC, JSON)
* MVX json package — portable (UniData/BASIC) MATJSONENCODE: encode a DIMENSIONED
* array as a JSON object per a MAPFIELD spec (the MATWRITE analogue of
* JSONENCODE, and the inverse of MATJSONDECODE).  The array subscript is the
* attribute position the spec maps, so A(pos) supplies what JSONENCODE reads
* from <pos>:
*   - a scalar field       -> A(pos)                      -> "key":value
*   - an association        -> A(pos) as a @VM list        -> "key":[{...},...]
* JSON returns the encoded object.  Typing / quoting / escaping / key-casing are
* the encoder's (see JSONENCODE); this only re-containers the record.  Trailing
* empty array elements are harmless — the encoder reads only mapped positions.
* GPL-2.0-only.
* JSONENCODE is a compiler intrinsic on mvx (native), a cataloged function on
* udt — so declare it only off-mvx.  MATPARSE/MATBUILD and MAT params are native
* on both, so this one source compiles for both platforms.
$IFNDEF MVX
   DEFFUN JSONENCODE(RX, SX)
$ENDIF
   MATBUILD R FROM A USING @AM
   JSON = JSONENCODE(R, SPEC)
   RETURN
